A glob view shows at most three frontmatter fields, `description` first and then `title`, then
the others in source order, with `...` when more follow; file mode prints them all, in source
order. A file with three fields or fewer shows them all, without `...`.
== args
input
== file input/many.md
---
b: 1
c: 2
title: Guide
d: 3
description: What this guide covers.
e: 4
---
# Guide
== file input/few.md
---
name: reviewer
description: Reviews code.
---
== stdout
glob view: input
input/few.md (4 lines): description: "Reviews code.", name: "reviewer"
input/many.md (9 lines): description: "What this guide covers.", title: "Guide", b: 1, ...
== stderr
== exit 0
